# bench/linux/linux-trimmed.fragment — D-0062 trimmed row.
# Merged onto the pinned board kernel config via merge_config.sh.
# One kconfig delta per line. Unset lines MUST be exactly
# "# CONFIG_X is not set" — merge_config.sh's SED_CONFIG_EXP2 is
# end-anchored, so a trailing note is not an unset. Notes go on the
# previous line and must not contain the string CONFIG_<SYM>:
# merge_config.sh uses grep -w CONFIG_X, and a note with that token
# becomes the "requested value".
#
# A symbol kconfig re-enables through a dependency is recorded as:
#   # merge-override SYM: <why it came back>
# merge_config.sh "redefined by fragment" is the fragment doing its
# job; linux-build prints it and does not require annotation.
# "Value requested for … not in final .config" has three cases:
#   fragment unset → final y: survival; annotate or abort
#   fragment unset → final absent: menu vanished; success
#   stock =y, not in this fragment, final absent: dependent drop;
#   success, no annotation (SCSI_MOD after BLOCK, …)
# requested-vs-final is case 1 on the fragment lines. Keeps
# (serial, virtio, IPv4 TCP, initramfs, DEVTMPFS, FUTEX) are
# asserted y on the final .config as their own check.
# Intent notes (`# FTRACE:`) are not merge-overrides.

# EXPERT: unhides BLOCK, PROC_FS, SYSFS, KALLSYMS, NAMESPACES
# (bool … if EXPERT, default y). Without it those unsets are
# invisible and olddefconfig restores y. On this board, EXPERT-only
# fallout is 86 new unsets plus PCIE_BUS_DEFAULT (does not survive
# PCI off). EPOLL and friends stay at stock defaults; we do not
# unset them. MODULES stays y: n retypes tristate as bool and
# canonicalizes m to y (symbol.c sym_get_type / calc_value).
CONFIG_EXPERT=y

## Keep: serial console (ttyS0 on the virt board UART)
CONFIG_TTY=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_OF_PLATFORM=y
# PRINTK: serial console implies it; quiet row silences with loglevel=0
CONFIG_PRINTK=y

## Keep: virtio-net over virtio-mmio, built in (no module loading without userspace)
CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MENU=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_NET=y

## Keep: IPv4 TCP only
CONFIG_NET=y
CONFIG_INET=y

## Keep: initramfs boot + static ELF /init
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
CONFIG_BINFMT_ELF=y
# DEVTMPFS: D-0062 keeps it; /init itself needs only the cpio console node
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
# FUTEX: static musl internals; not worth the breakage risk
CONFIG_FUTEX=y

## Off: no v6, no storage, no second boot path
# IPV6: IPv4 only
# CONFIG_IPV6 is not set
# BLOCK: initramfs, no storage
# CONFIG_BLOCK is not set
# PCI: virtio here is MMIO; the virt board boots without PCI
# CONFIG_PCI is not set
# EFI: OpenSBI + -kernel; no EFI stub on this path
# CONFIG_EFI is not set
# merge-override EFI: arch/riscv/Kconfig `config PORTABLE` (default !NONPORTABLE) `select EFI`. This tree has PORTABLE=y; unsetting EFI requires NONPORTABLE, which is a board-personality change we will not make.

## Off: single hart (matches the fixed machine shape; listed as tuning)
# SMP: QEMU -smp 1; matches the fixed machine shape
# CONFIG_SMP is not set

## Off: determinism / boot cost
# RANDOMIZE_BASE: KASLR
# CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE is not set
# IKCONFIG: no /proc/config.gz
# CONFIG_IKCONFIG is not set
# KALLSYMS: no symbol table in the image
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set

## Off: no userspace beyond /init
# UNIX: no AF_UNIX; /init talks TCP
# CONFIG_UNIX is not set
# PACKET: announce is UDP-to-gateway, not AF_PACKET (D-0062 amendment)
# CONFIG_PACKET is not set
# PROC_FS: aggressive; first re-enable candidate on no-boot
# CONFIG_PROC_FS is not set
# SYSFS: aggressive; second re-enable candidate on no-boot
# CONFIG_SYSFS is not set
# TMPFS: rootfs stays ramfs
# CONFIG_TMPFS is not set
# SWAP: no backing store (vanishes from .config when BLOCK is off)
# CONFIG_SWAP is not set
# NAMESPACES: single task, no isolation knobs
# CONFIG_NAMESPACES is not set
# CGROUPS: no controllers, no userspace to configure them
# CONFIG_CGROUPS is not set

## Off: D-0073 — named miss plus printk-visible leftovers
# FTRACE: menuconfig Tracers; defaults y if DEBUG_KERNEL; not EXPERT.
# D-0072 named trace_eval_sync as 68% of the 327 ms hole. Missed trim.
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
# NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS: NFS / 9P_FS / SUNRPC menu. Does not cover
# the 9p transport (that is NET_9P, under NET).
# CONFIG_NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS is not set
# NET_9P: 9p has a filesystem under the network-filesystems menu
# and a 9P2000 transport under networking. Killing the fs menu
# does not kill the transport. T4.8: "9pnet: Installing 9P2000
# support"; p9_virtio_init / p9_trans_fd_init.
# CONFIG_NET_9P is not set
# DNS_RESOLVER: NFS v4 selected it; the prompt sits under
# networking options, not the network-filesystems menu. T4.8 hole
# started at "Key type dns_resolver registered".
# CONFIG_DNS_RESOLVER is not set
# NLS: FAT/ISO went with BLOCK; USB (which selected the NLS
# core) went with USB_SUPPORT. Native language support is a
# different parent; the prompt keeps it y. T4.8: init_nls_cp437.
# CONFIG_NLS is not set
# MTD: MTD_BLOCK went with BLOCK; the MTD core does not.
# CONFIG_MTD is not set
# DAX: PMEM/NVDIMM went with BLOCK (LIBNVDIMM depends on
# BLK_DEV). Direct-access is a different menu; the prompt
# keeps it y. T4.8: dax_core_init.
# CONFIG_DAX is not set
# IP_PNP: kernel IP autoconfig exists to serve NFS root /
# diskless boot. ROOT_NFS went with the network-filesystems
# menu; this prompt sits under IPv4. /init does SIOCSIFADDR
# itself. T4.8: ip_auto_config.
# CONFIG_IP_PNP is not set
# FHANDLE: default-y EXPERT prompt; selects the fs-export helper.
# /init never name_to_handle_at. Unsetting the helper alone
# leaves it m because this prompt still selects it.
# CONFIG_FHANDLE is not set
# OVERLAY_FS: the other live selector of the fs-export helper
# (defconfig m). Same: unsetting the helper alone leaves it m.
# CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS is not set
# EXPORTFS: bare tristate in fs/Kconfig, no menu. NFSD selected
# it; FHANDLE and overlay still did after NFSD vanished.
# Non-reversing select: killing a selector does not unset the
# target.
# CONFIG_EXPORTFS is not set
# KEYS: D-0073 originally said keep; superseded after
# NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS removed the only selector.
# Only live selector was NFS_V4. /init never touches a keyring.
# CONFIG_KEYS is not set
# MEMFD_CREATE: EXPERT prompt, no default; selected by TMPFS
# and HUGETLBFS, both already unset. The prompt kept it y.
# CONFIG_MEMFD_CREATE is not set
# EEPROM_93CX6: selected by SERIAL_8250_EXAR (PCI), now gone.
# CONFIG_EEPROM_93CX6 is not set
# EXTCON: selected by USB_PHY; USB already off. Charger-manager
# is not a remaining consumer.
# CONFIG_EXTCON is not set
# INPUT_FF_MEMLESS: selected by HID force-feedback drivers;
# HID already unset.
# CONFIG_INPUT_FF_MEMLESS is not set
# HID_SUPPORT: menuconfig default y wrapping HID. Same split as
# USB_SUPPORT: we unset the bus, the menu parent stayed.
# CONFIG_HID_SUPPORT is not set
# REALTEK_PHY: selected by R8169, which died with PCI. (MICREL
# still serves MACB; that is not this pattern.)
# CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY is not set
# SPI_MEM: selected by MTD_SPI_NOR; MTD already unset.
# CONFIG_SPI_MEM is not set
# NETWORK_SECMARK: selected by SELinux, which cascaded off.
# CONFIG_NETWORK_SECMARK is not set
# SECURITYFS: selected by AppArmor/IMA; SECURITY already absent.
# The prompt kept it y.
# CONFIG_SECURITYFS is not set
# USB_SUPPORT: host USB / usbhid. No USB on this virt path.
# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
# SOUND: ALSA. T4.8: "No soundcards found."
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# MMC: SDHCI / dwmmc. No card, no BLOCK backing.
# CONFIG_MMC is not set
# INPUT_MOUSEDEV: "mousedev: PS/2 mouse device common for all mice"
# CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSEDEV is not set
# INPUT_MOUSE: psmouse and friends; no mice on this machine.
# CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSE is not set
# HID: leftover HID core once USB is off.
# CONFIG_HID is not set
# HUGETLBFS: HugeTLB registered 2 MiB, pre-allocated 0. Unused.
# CONFIG_HUGETLBFS is not set
# AUDIT: netlink audit initialized disabled. No LSM consumer here.
# CONFIG_AUDIT is not set
# BPF_SYSCALL: hole is full of bpf_* initcalls; /init never bpf().
# CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL is not set
# ACPI: T4.8 "ACPI: Interpreter disabled." DT boot, not ACPI.
# CONFIG_ACPI is not set
# PNP: "PnP ACPI: disabled"
# CONFIG_PNP is not set
# LEGACY_PTYS: BSD ptys; not EXPERT-gated; default y; unused.
# CONFIG_LEGACY_PTYS is not set
# UNIX98_PTYS: EXPERT-gated default y (unlike FTRACE). EXPERT is already
# on. pty_init was 33.8 ms UART-inflated on the diagnostic boot.
# CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS is not set
# RTC_CLASS: goldfish_rtc registered as rtc0 and set the wall clock.
# /init uses CLOCK_MONOTONIC (riscv clocksource), not rtc0.
# CONFIG_RTC_CLASS is not set
# WATCHDOG: watchdog_init was 8.0 ms UART-inflated. No watchdog userspace.
# CONFIG_WATCHDOG is not set

# Deferred this pass (named so they are not found one at a time):
# VT, DEBUG_FS, FB, PINCTRL, I2C / SPI / GPIO, thermal, cpuidle,
# LSM (SELinux / AppArmor). Either already off (SYSFS unset), not
# obviously unused without a no-boot risk, or idle-path rather than a
# named leftover. Second-look the actual trimmed.config before the
# campaign.

# SBI SRST poweroff needs no explicit symbol on the pinned kernel;
# the boot gate proves it, and if the pinned version disagrees, the
# needed symbol joins this list with a comment.
